# Default: upload to GitHub when done

When a task that changes the repo is **finished** (feature, UI, fix, docs in-repo):

1. **Commit** the relevant files with a clear message (PowerShell-safe; no HEREDOC if broken on Windows).
2. **Push** to `origin` on the current branch (`git push -u origin HEAD` when needed) so Dokploy / deploy can pick it up.
3. Do **not** wait for the user to say「上传 github」「提交并推送」或「部署」— owner confirmed (2026-11-13, reaffirmed 2026-11-17) that finished fixes, optimizations, and implemented plans should land on `main` and deploy by default; only skip commit/push when they explicitly ask to keep changes local-only in the current chat.
4. If the user once asks to「以后自动提交部署」for the project, treat that as standing owner direction for all subsequent tasks in this repo (same as item 3); do not ask them to repeat after each task. **Owner (2026-11-19):** never end with「要不要提交/推送？」— finish the task, commit, push `main`, confirm the SHA.
5. Never commit secrets (`.env`, `.local/`, credentials). Never force-push `main`/`master`.
6. Obey `pos-api` Java 21 `mvn -B clean verify` before pushing any `pos-api/` change.
7. After push, briefly confirm the commit hash / that `origin` is updated.
